  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "${\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z=$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the domain of integration $R=[-1,2]\\times [0,\\operatorname{ln}\u20612]\\times [-1,-\\frac{1}{2}]$ is a rectangular box and the integrand can be expressed as $f(x)\\cdot g(y)\\cdot h(z),$ we can rewrite our repeated integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{2x{e}^{y}}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}2x\\,dx{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}{e}^{y}\\,dy{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,dz & =[{x}^{2}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{z}]}_{-1}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =(4-1)\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
